+## Rebase onto the receiver lead v4rxg3 (2026-11-02)
+
+The router sources are now v4rxg3's (main tree `fabric_exp/variants/v4rxg3`: channel-kind names, `ReceiverChannelStates`
+with the derived `loop_local_vc`, `DownstreamConnections`, per-VC feature arrays, the buffer-2 fix (c)), with VC2 line
+mode re-applied in its vocabulary. Snapshot: `fabric_exp/variants/vc2l_g3a`. The 1D line-VC host and the 29 KiB buffer
+stay.
+
+### What VC2 line mode is in g3's terms (device)
+
+- A VC2 line receiver channel is `ReceiverChannel<2>` like any other: `forwards` from the host's
+  `DISABLE_RX_CH2_FORWARDING` (0 in line mode, so the `delivers_only` edit is gone), first-level acks from
+  `ENABLE_FIRST_LEVEL_ACK_VC2`, crossover from `VC2_CROSSOVER_TO_VC1` (`forwards_on_vc`), its state placed by
+  `ReceiverChannelStates` (VC0 is the loop-local VC wherever it runs). The receiver has no VC2 code; its only edit is the
+  trimming capture's per-VC table of packed downstream ids (three entries).
+- Per-VC line routing: ct `is_vc_routed_as_line[MAX_NUM_VCS]` from the host's `VC<n>_ROUTES_AS_LINE` (the 1D line-VC
+  host's format-neutral words; `VC2_LINE_MODE` is no longer read). `vc_routes_as_line(vc)` = 2D and that bit; a
+  static_assert says only VC2 can be one on a 2D fabric, which is why the line's two stream ids below are VC2's.
+- router_common.hpp: `receiver_channel_of(vc)` (moved from the receiver: the downstream traits use it), `vc_routes_as_line`,
+  `opposite_direction`, the line branches of the two downstream stream-id functions.
+- router_downstream.hpp: three entries in `DOWNSTREAM_EDM_COUNT_BY_VC`; the traits' command buffers are the VC's receiver
+  channel's (`receiver_channel_of(VC)`; the same ids as g3's `[VC]` for VC0 and VC1); a line VC's live set is the
+  opposite direction; `vc_forwards_to_routers(2)` where VC2 routes as a line; `DownstreamConnections::vc2` (Present) and
+  `of<2>()`. The shared preset is g3's rule unchanged, extended over VC2: VC0 keeps its preset unless VC1 or VC2
+  clobbers it, and a VC2 line whose live set equals VC0's rides it; `forwards_set_credit_register` when VC1 or VC2 rides.
+  The VC2-specific `command_channel` and `line_vc_shares_vc0_preset` of p3b are gone.
+- router_routing.hpp: a line VC's route that turns stops watcher builds (Route's constructor; `turns()` accessor gone).
+- router_init.hpp: VC2's runtime-arg block (Present, after VC1's; teardown words after VC1's), init in
+  `init_downstream_connections`.
+- router_sender.hpp: p3b's VC2 forwarding channel (mask, record, visit after VC2's worker) and the bubble-flow-control
+  assert; g3's sender already read `is_vc_first_level_ack_enabled`.
+- fabric_erisc_router_ct_args.hpp: `VC2_FREE_SLOTS_FROM_DOWNSTREAM_STREAM_ID`, `NUM_DOWNSTREAM_SENDERS_VC2`,
+  `VC2_DOWNSTREAM_EDM_SIZE`, `OPEN_DOWNSTREAM_VC2_CONNECTIONS`, `PACKED_DOWNSTREAM_VC2_SENDER_CHANNEL_IDS`,
+  `is_vc_routed_as_line`, and the transaction-ID rule for three receiver channels (4 each under deadlock avoidance, with
+  its static_assert).
+- fabric_erisc_router_v2.cpp: the gate. Neighbour exchange keeps g3's (`!has_vc1`, one sender channel, forwarding off,
+  no VC2 acks or crossover); line mode: two VC2 sender channels on a cardinal router, VC1 allowed, acks and crossover
+  from the host. VC2's downstream connection opens after VC1's (`OPEN_DOWNSTREAM_VC2_CONNECTIONS`).
+- Consequence of g3's gate: VC1 + VC2 neighbour exchange (v4rxc7v's test) does not compile (as on the lead), so the
+  `mm_sanity_nbr` step is out.
+
+### Host
+
+- `VC2_CROSSOVER_TO_VC1` = VC0's crossover and VC2 forwards (the fact the host already computed for
+  `RX_CH_<r>_FORWARDS_ON_VC`). The host's `ENABLE_FIRST_LEVEL_ACK_VC2` was already set by mode.
+- vc2l_offline.py injects `VC<n>_ROUTES_AS_LINE` (VC2's from `VC2_LINE_MODE`) and `VC2_CROSSOVER_TO_VC1` (from
+  `RX_CH_<r>_FORWARDS_ON_VC`) into captures that predate them.
