+## Phase 5 plan (proposed 2026-11-02; waits for the user's decision)
+
+Two or more cabled Galaxies: VC2 rings spanning hosts, and multi-mesh across hosts. Allocation: the 110-a pod partitions
+(`bh_sc36_6_110a_pod1`..`pod9`, `_lp`; a pod is four Galaxies, e.g. pod7 = bh-glx-110-a01u02/08/14/20), `--nodes=2`
+first. Open for the coordinator: whether a two-node job counts as one of the study's 4 concurrent allocations.
+
+1. Offline first (CPU): mock captures on the repo's two-Galaxy descriptors (`dual_glx_2.5d_torus`,
+   `dual_bh_galaxy_experimental`) with `16x4_dual_bh_galaxy_2d_mesh` (one 16x4 mesh over two hosts) and
+   `dual_bh_galaxy_torus_xy` (8x8 torus over two hosts), VC2 line mode: placement (VC2 line excludes Z routers, so the
+   host link must be cardinal on the chosen descriptor), router sizes, yaml vets.
+2. Harness (`vc2l_glx_mh.sbatch`, dry-run with stubs, normal and hang paths): on every node, via `srun` one task per
+   node, the node guard (`bh-glx-110-a*`), the busy check, `tt-smi -glx_reset`, and on a timeout the kill of this job's
+   processes and a hang capture; MPI between hosts over TCP with an explicit interface (the shared-memory setting of the
+   split cannot cross hosts; job 167436's TCP start-up stall says to pick the interface and to run a two-rank MPI preflight
+   across the nodes before any device work); per-rank kernel caches (done); the tree on /data as now.
+3. Connectivity smoke (VC0 only, existing suites) on the chosen descriptor, since the cabling in tt-cluster-config may
+   be stale: stop and report if links are missing.
+4. Rings spanning hosts, data-checked: VC2 line rings along the axis that crosses the hosts (wrap unicast, full-ring
+   multicast, both directions from every chip, next to VC0 torus traffic; a 2-slot VC2 ring stress), two ERISCs and one;
+   then the short torus stability suite with VC2 line mode.
+5. Multi-mesh across hosts, data-checked: each Galaxy one 8x4 mesh, VC0/VC1 multi-mesh sanity, VC2 fan-in into VC1
+   over the host link, and all three VCs at once (an allvc yaml for 8x4 meshes, VC2 sources in line with the exits the
+   mock shows, as for the 4x4 split).
+6. Then four Galaxies (a quad) if two work; a first perf look only after the data checks.
